Interpretation
  * Exact sigma, not the raw cyclic label winding, detects tooth escape.
  * The first liar already has one winding and pure endpoint ownership; metric width/phase is indispensable.
  * Component tournaments retain within-tooth phase order but still quotient away sigma's width term.
  * Challenge to the vertex assumption: components are more faithful than runners, yet a proof object must
    carry (component interval, endpoint owners, tooth phase, width, deletion deck), not only a tournament.
